==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[white]] [[noise]]|-}}
{{examples-right|examples={{audio|White noise.ogg|10s of white noise|lang=en}}}}

# {{context|physics|lang=en}} A [[random]] [[signal]] (or [[process]]) with a [[flat]] [[power]] [[spectral]] [[density]]; a signal with a power spectral density that has equal power in any [[band]], at any centre frequency, having a given bandwidth.
#* '''2005''', John G. Holden, ''[http://www.nsf.gov/sbe/bcs/pac/nmbs/chap6.pdf Gauging the Fractal Dimension of Response Times from Cognitive Tasks]''
#*: Conventional statistical analyses presuppose that intrinsic variability is '''white noise'''.  '''White noise''' yields a jagged and irregular line with a fractal dimension of 1.5, because successive observations are statistically independent of each other. 
# {{context|nontechnically|lang=en}} Any [[nondescript]] [[noise]] used for [[background]] or to [[mask]] or [[drown out]] other noise.

